	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/uco/Mutex"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "A mutex is a mechanism that enforces limits on access to a resource when there are many threads of execution. A mutex is designed to enforce a mutual exclusion concurrency control policy, and with a variety of possible methods there exists multiple unique implementations for different applications. [based on https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lock_(computer_science)]" ;
